So far we have considered the two pairs of vHs – occupied and unoccupied – separately. The reasoning is that
the energy separation between these pairs, of the order
of 200 meV [see Fig. 1(c)], is significant enough that it
is likely to prevent instabilities driven by the coupling
between states associated with occupied and unoccupied
vHs. Nevertheless, it is possible that this energy splitting
could be reduced by correlations not captured by DFT,
or by different doping schemes. Moreover, even within
DFT, upon moving away from the M point along the
M − L line, the energy splitting between the pairs of vHs
changes as a function of out-of-plane momentum [8].
Therefore, and for the sake of completeness, we briefly
discuss the properties of the possible iCDW order parameters obtained by combining states from vHs above
and below the Fermi level. The only combinations that
give iCDW orders not already discussed above are the
symmetric and anti-symmetric inter-orbital iCDW order
